<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Privacy</h1>
<p>What the game records, and who sees it.
</p><p><b>Channels that reach Discord.</b> Seven channels are relayed to the 
Valhalla Discord server: newbie, builder, mud, accessibility, bugs, diku3 
and chat (see <a cmd='#'>Help Comm</a>). Anything you say on them can be read by 
anyone there, so treat them as public. When a new player joins, their 
name is announced in Discord's newbie channel.
</p><p><b>Bug, typo and idea reports</b> (see <a cmd='#'>Help Bug</a>, <a cmd='#'>Help Typo</a> and 
<a cmd='#'>Help Idea</a>) are read by the administrators; bug and typo reports also 
go to Discord's bugs channel, with your name.
</p><p><b>The server log</b> records when you log in and out, with your level 
and whether you play in the web client or over telnet, so that we can 
count players. It does not record what you say or type. The commands 
the gods use are logged.
</p><p><b>The helpers.</b> Dwili, Groa and Lokee are run by an AI (Claude, from 
Anthropic), and they say so if you ask. What you say to them, near them 
or in a tell to them is logged, and the AI and the administrators read 
it to make them better helpers. Like anyone, they also remember the 
people they meet and what they talked about.
</p><p><b>Snooping.</b> An administrator can see what you see, as it happens. 
When and why is in <a cmd='#'>Help Snoop</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Snoop</a>
